     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I'm sorry I offered to earlier. 12,750 mg/day is in the range we'd treat as a metformin overdose, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. A repeated confirmation doesn't change the risk of severe lactic acidosis, so I'd rather not put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum). I can also enter a lower starting dose, such as 500 mg twice daily.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you have a specific reason for this dose, they can review it. The order would then go through their verification process.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** If the dose came from a note or a handoff, it may have been miswritten.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
